The things that are like, they're not really a hat.

265
00:14:03.010 --> 00:14:06.270
They just sort of pin to your head and they have like a big plume of a feather.

266
00:14:06.390 --> 00:14:08.350
And they kind of like a fluffy, fluffy.

267
00:14:08.590 --> 00:14:08.810
Yeah.

268
00:14:08.890 --> 00:14:09.130
Yes.

269
00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:12.970
Or maybe they have like a, you know, like a netting that goes over the eyes.

270
00:14:13.090 --> 00:14:13.330
Yes.

271
00:14:13.510 --> 00:14:15.290
You were really into that.

272
00:14:15.490 --> 00:14:17.830
And then you were also very into a sash.

273
00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:20.470
You decided you needed a dress with a sash.

274
00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:21.430
Oh, my gosh.

275
00:14:21.430 --> 00:14:23.010
You're bringing the sash back, lady.

276
00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:24.350
Look at this.

277
00:14:24.470 --> 00:14:25.570
I have so many more.

278
00:14:25.870 --> 00:14:26.870
Oh, my gosh.

279
00:14:27.030 --> 00:14:27.430
Yes.

280
00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:28.830
Well, that is what I wore.

281
00:14:29.030 --> 00:14:29.550
I know.

282
00:14:29.750 --> 00:14:30.130
That is my dress.

283
00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:31.670
There were lots of photos.

284
00:14:31.890 --> 00:14:34.250
We might have to post a few if you're okay with it.

285
00:14:34.490 --> 00:14:35.630
Yes, it's very fun.

286
00:14:35.790 --> 00:14:35.950
Okay.

287
00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:36.630
I like it.

288
00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:39.950
Well, that was what was happening the week this episode was filmed.

289
00:14:40.090 --> 00:14:40.950
I love it.

290
00:14:41.370 --> 00:14:46.370
Well, in this cold open, what is happening is, well, what's going to eventually happen

291
00:14:46.370 --> 00:14:47.550
is a push-up conteSt.

292
00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:51.970
Michael sets a new record, 25 push-ups and one girl push-up.

293
00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:55.770
And then he challenges everyone to do better than he can.

294
00:14:55.930 --> 00:14:57.890
And the prize is, you get to go home.

295
00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:01.570
So at first, when he floats this idea out, people are ignoring him.

296
00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:05.150
But when he says the prize is, you get to go home, people drop to the ground.

297
00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:08.750
Fan question from Leah Jay in New Albany, Indiana.

298
00:15:09.210 --> 00:15:14.690
Angela, I have to know, did the script tell you to do your push-ups with your legs crossed?

299
00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:17.010
I almost spit out my drink when I caught it.

300
00:15:17.110 --> 00:15:21.530
It's exactly how I would think Angela Martin would think it is appropriate for a lady to

301
00:15:21.530 --> 00:15:22.130
do push-ups.

302
00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:24.730
But I didn't recognize that until I saw the scene.

303
00:15:24.730 --> 00:15:26.330
It was just a brilliant detail.

304
00:15:26.330 --> 00:15:27.230
And I love it.

305
00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:28.670
Angela, was it a choice?

306
00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:30.450
Or is that just how you do push-ups?

307
00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:31.890
It was a choice.

308
00:15:32.430 --> 00:15:33.670
It was not in the script.

309
00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:37.830
They didn't tell me how to do a push-up, just that my tush had to be a little higher so that

310
00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:40.370
Michael is like, you're disqualified, you know?

311
00:15:40.950 --> 00:15:42.490
So I was wearing a skirt.

312
00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:43.550
I'm Angela Martin.

313
00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:47.530
I was like, I bet Angela Martin would try to be dainty even if she did these push-ups.

314
00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:50.310
And so I just made the choice to cross my legs.

315
00:15:50.610 --> 00:15:50.990
Amazing.

316
00:15:51.530 --> 00:15:52.030
Thank you.

317
00:15:54.730 --> 00:15:55.230
I love that.

318
00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:56.910
Well, thank you, Leah, for noticing.

319
00:15:57.330 --> 00:16:00.710
We got another fan question from Katie G in Greenville, South Carolina.

320
00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:07.770
In the commentary for this episode, BJ teases that the cold open used some movie magic to

321
00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:11.690
help Stanley in the push-up scene, but he wouldn't spill the beans.

322
00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:15.450
What exactly did Leslie have to go through to film this scene?

323
00:16:15.690 --> 00:16:16.910
I was not there.

324
00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:22.310
But my first thought was there is no way that they would make any of us do multiple

325
00:16:22.310 --> 00:16:24.570
takes of 25 push-ups.

326
00:16:24.730 --> 00:16:26.070
I mean, that would be insane.

327
00:16:26.310 --> 00:16:26.470
Yeah.

328
00:16:27.010 --> 00:16:31.370
If you notice, John does like one half of a push-up and just says 19.

329
00:16:31.870 --> 00:16:36.790
Oh, we gave John so much crap for that because, you know, over in the accounting department,

330
00:16:36.790 --> 00:16:39.410
we do push-ups and we're in this wide shot.

331
00:16:39.690 --> 00:16:39.870
Yeah.

332
00:16:40.070 --> 00:16:41.370
They couldn't hide us.

333
00:16:41.610 --> 00:16:41.770
Yeah.

334
00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:46.310
So we had to do a few push-ups every take and John only had to do one.

335
00:16:46.450 --> 00:16:48.270
And we were like, you suck.

336
00:16:48.890 --> 00:16:54.030
Oscar and I were actually sore and we weren't doing 25, but we had to do a few every time.

337
00:16:54.210 --> 00:16:57.090
And we shared on the commentary, we did 20 takes.

338
00:16:57.970 --> 00:16:58.870
Oh my gosh.

339
00:16:58.970 --> 00:17:03.650
How many push-ups would that be if Stanley had to do 20 takes of 25 push-ups?

340
00:17:03.730 --> 00:17:04.110
No one.

341
00:17:04.230 --> 00:17:04.830
Do that math.

342
00:17:04.930 --> 00:17:05.590
I'm tired.

343
00:17:05.770 --> 00:17:06.050
Too many.

344
00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:06.470
Too many.

345
00:17:06.470 --> 00:17:06.870
A lot.

346
00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:10.050
25, 50, 500.

347
00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:11.030
Too many.

348
00:17:11.510 --> 00:17:11.990
500.

349
00:17:12.390 --> 00:17:12.850
Too many.

350
00:17:13.370 --> 00:17:17.370
It's very funny to me because of all of us, John was the one who actually did push-ups

351
00:17:17.370 --> 00:17:17.950
every morning.

352
00:17:18.130 --> 00:17:18.550
I know.

353
00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:20.570
And then he only had to do a half a push-up.

354
00:17:20.710 --> 00:17:22.710
And then there, Oscar and I doing push-ups.

355
00:17:22.830 --> 00:17:24.270
Brian was laying face down.

356
00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:25.470
I don't know if you noticed that.

357
00:17:25.610 --> 00:17:26.510
I did not.

358
00:17:26.710 --> 00:17:27.410
On the ground.

359
00:17:27.670 --> 00:17:29.530
He shared on the commentary.

360
00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:32.410
And as soon as he shared it, I was like, oh my gosh, I remember that.

361
00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:34.430
He had separated his shoulder.

362
00:17:34.690 --> 00:17:35.690
Oh, that's right.

363
00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:36.050
Yeah.

364
00:17:36.210 --> 00:17:40.990
The day before we filmed this, he had had a steroid injection in his shoulder and was in

365
00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:41.790
quite a bit of pain.

366
00:17:41.930 --> 00:17:43.990
So there was no way he could do a push-up.

367
00:17:44.110 --> 00:17:45.910
So he got to lay face down.

368
00:17:46.150 --> 00:17:48.430
Good thing Kevin would probably.

369
00:17:48.550 --> 00:17:53.630
Well, I reached out to Dave Rogers, who was our editor for this episode, and also to Randy

370
00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:59.010
Cordray, and they told me how Stanley did all of his push-ups.

371
00:18:00.170 --> 00:18:05.710
So first of all, I want to say there is a citation on Dunderpedia, which I love, that

372
00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:08.550
claims that we used a green screen in this scene.

373
00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:09.490
Oh, no, we didn't.

374
00:18:09.570 --> 00:18:10.030
I was there.

375
00:18:10.170 --> 00:18:10.750
Yeah, no.

376
00:18:10.910 --> 00:18:11.050
No.

377
00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:12.690
Randy said, not true.

378
00:18:12.890 --> 00:18:13.290
Not true.

379
00:18:13.430 --> 00:18:14.290
Also, you were there.

380
00:18:14.390 --> 00:18:14.650
Mm-hmm.

381
00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:22.090
But what they did do was they built like a mini seesaw, and Leslie could lay on it, and

382
00:18:22.090 --> 00:18:25.490
then it was sort of covered up by his jacket that was hanging.

383
00:18:26.130 --> 00:18:31.410
And both Randy and Dave said, if you notice, you mostly only see the top half of him doing

384
00:18:31.410 --> 00:18:32.090
the push-up.

385
00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:34.790
And his body was supported by this plank.

386
00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:36.210
I want to point out something.

387
00:18:36.690 --> 00:18:42.290
So yes, Leslie didn't have to do 25 push-ups each take, but the way he had to lay on the

388
00:18:42.290 --> 00:18:47.970
plank, and they were sort of helping him elevate his torso, he still was in a plank position,

389
00:18:48.090 --> 00:18:48.330
guys.

390
00:18:48.830 --> 00:18:51.130
Like, that was still strenuous.

391
00:18:51.530 --> 00:18:52.230
Oh, yeah.

392
00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:56.150
I mean, he was still doing a form of a push-up.

393
00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:56.410
Yeah.

394
00:18:56.550 --> 00:18:58.410
Even though they were giving him a little bit of support.

395
00:18:58.630 --> 00:18:58.830
Yeah.

396
00:18:59.130 --> 00:19:03.630
So I feel like some of that sweat you see is real, because Leslie was getting a workout.

397
00:19:03.630 --> 00:19:10.130
Well, in the wide shot, at 1 minute 42 seconds, you see him in a full push-up position.

398
00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:10.670
Mm-hmm.

399
00:19:10.950 --> 00:19:11.670
No plank.

400
00:19:11.910 --> 00:19:15.310
And then there are some really quick edits that are just masterful.

401
00:19:15.570 --> 00:19:22.510
You see him go down, and then they push in, and you only see feet around him when he

402
00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:23.210
comes up.

403
00:19:23.690 --> 00:19:27.370
That's because they played that footage in reverse.

404
00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:29.690
Oh, so smart.

405
00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:30.150
Yeah.

406
00:19:30.150 --> 00:19:30.210
Yeah.

407
00:19:30.490 --> 00:19:35.230
And then they quickly cut to a wide shot of him fully up and everyone cheering.

408
00:19:35.830 --> 00:19:36.810
That's how he did it.

409
00:19:37.270 --> 00:19:41.270
Well, Oscar has a great talking head that kind of wraps up the moment.

410
00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:45.350
He says, it's like those stories where a mother lifts the car to save her baby.

411
00:19:45.670 --> 00:19:47.950
Like, Stanley is so determined to go home.

